{"title":"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Contest_Solution,_most_recommended_and_fastest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Contest Solution, most recommended and fastest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Fast_with_no_explanations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Fast with no explanations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One-inch squares are cut from the corners of this 5 inch square.  What is the area in square inches of the largest square that can be fitted into the remaining space?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/16905c0611e83380a7ff4045538ffe74a49c7cb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(75); draw((0,0)--(0,5)--(5,5)--(5,0)--cycle); filldraw((0,4)--(1,4)--(1,5)--(0,5)--cycle, gray); filldraw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle, gray); filldraw((4,0)--(4,1)--(5,1)--(5,0)--cycle, gray); filldraw((4,4)--(4,5)--(5,5)--(5,4)--cycle, gray); [/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a50665010dfc0abf15aacdb80a728fb3e41e28cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)  } 9\\qquad \\textbf{(B)  } 12\\frac{1}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)  } 15\\qquad \\textbf{(D)  } 15\\frac{1}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)  } 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"418\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can draw a diagram as shown:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f3c48a29012ff643c122bc29fed89b069d59e9c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(75); draw((0,0)--(0,5)--(5,5)--(5,0)--cycle); filldraw((0,4)--(1,4)--(1,5)--(0,5)--cycle, gray); filldraw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle, gray); filldraw((4,0)--(4,1)--(5,1)--(5,0)--cycle, gray); filldraw((4,4)--(4,5)--(5,5)--(5,4)--cycle, gray); path arc = arc((2.5,4),1.5,0,90); pair P = intersectionpoint(arc,(0,5)--(5,5)); pair Pp=rotate(90,(2.5,2.5))*P, Ppp = rotate(90,(2.5,2.5))*Pp, Pppp=rotate(90,(2.5,2.5))*Ppp; draw(P--Pp--Ppp--Pppp--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"125\" /> \nLet us focus on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> big triangles that, together with the inscribed square, fill in the large square. If we zoom in on one of the four triangles, we can see that it is composed of a small unit square in the corner of the large square and two triangles, one smaller than the other. We are going to focus specifically on the smaller of the two triangles. This triangle is similar to the big triangle itself by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed7b97f90f271cacdec9cdb730fdadf133407acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{AA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> similarity (because the two sides of a square are parallel. To prove this fact, draw a diagonal of the square and find congruent triangles). Let the shorter leg of the big triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />; then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d43b34249e23b01bb9cc89befec7517bb614378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x}{x-1}=\\dfrac{5-x}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c77d96e62cdcd23bf81e073e0148887e1bf01d80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=-x^2+6x-5\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f26da441af2f91c38eb4fb47b5886d5da9775b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2-5x+5=0\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/946c0be301e9cbfa5e5802f3eaa1f29d4083b560.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\dfrac{5\\pm \\sqrt{(-5)^2-(4)(1)(5)}}{2}\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/61327043a82f4aa7c550aee56bbea0ba47e9a91e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\dfrac{5\\pm \\sqrt{5}}{2}\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/2978530493b8758d858726ebe653c0a75846f4ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\dfrac{5-\\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"43\" />, because by symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/813e12ee527f4b85c857468734aca5b27d51d1a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; \\dfrac52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />. Note that the other solution we got, namely, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e1852312a1386ade3b1ba24ab337e458454191.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\dfrac{5+\\sqrt 5} 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" />, is the length of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c445a843f7b9a5ae5e089d62c7a3d22d55a9bee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-x$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c445a843f7b9a5ae5e089d62c7a3d22d55a9bee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-x$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> together sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the side of the length of the large square, and similarly, the sum of the solutions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This solution is a result of the symmetry of the problem; if we had set the longer leg of the big triangle to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then we would solve the same quadratic to find the same roots, the only difference being that we take the other root.\n</p><p>This means the area of each triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8eef00b53278b8b811972e5567708f943d9f8fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{5-\\sqrt{5}}{2}*(5-\\dfrac{5-\\sqrt{5}}{2})*\\dfrac{1}{2}=\\dfrac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"247\" height=\"41\" />.\nThus, the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d152ca7c4faca8127bad65fe33773890fff3f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25-(4*\\dfrac{5}{2})=15\\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"226\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Don't use this in a contest scenario, and only use it when practicing math skills.&#160;:)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Contest_Solution.2C_most_recommended_and_fastest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Contest_Solution,_most_recommended_and_fastest)\">Solution 2 (Contest Solution, most recommended and fastest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Contest Solution, most recommended and fastest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We draw a square as shown:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a4e93cbdad64505b459860b8645b93a54f23cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(75); draw((0,0)--(0,5)--(5,5)--(5,0)--cycle);  filldraw((0,4)--(1,4)--(1,5)--(0,5)--cycle, gray);  filldraw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle, gray);  filldraw((4,0)--(4,1)--(5,1)--(5,0)--cycle, gray);  filldraw((4,4)--(4,5)--(5,5)--(5,4)--cycle, gray);  path arc = arc((2.5,4),1.5,0,90);  pair P = intersectionpoint(arc,(0,5)--(5,5));  pair Pp=rotate(90,(2.5,2.5))*P, Ppp = rotate(90,(2.5,2.5))*Pp, Pppp=rotate(90,(2.5,2.5))*Ppp;  draw(P--Pp--Ppp--Pppp--cycle);  filldraw((1,4)--P--(4,4)--cycle,red); filldraw((4,4)--Pppp--(4,1)--cycle,red); filldraw((1,1)--Ppp--(4,1)--cycle,red); filldraw((1,1)--Pp--(1,4)--cycle,red); [/asy]\" width=\"125\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe want to find the area of the biggest square. The area of this square is composed of the center white square and the four red triangles. Because the inner square has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d976d4e4d7a8c512c5e94b30337e0c01887a685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, squared, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it also has a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dcba07bde5741ce967fc1b96296720f986e6375.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{9}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />. The heights of each of the red triangles are 1 (because the gray squares have lengths of one), and the area of one triangle is namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a12c7b8106d6f3221fb7fe6b1f202382f13bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 \\cdot 1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, the combined area of the four triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b68f06c479a39e62f7f3479765c7adb789fec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot \\frac 32=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" />. Furthermore, the area of the smaller square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We add these to see that the area of the large square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4ddaccd7bbcffc6d5a1b688bc514ee0c1b84f7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+6=15\\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"172\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us find the area of the triangles and the unit squares: on each side, there are two triangles. They both have one leg of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and let's label the other legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for one of the triangles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> for the other. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76aa8b8c4b979e876acb7aef5e3304c795491f99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />.\nThe area of each of the triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876fba774d252c254bd1496f6a44b4db630e55cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"16\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e741dac04a81604d228dae39e8f7f29819647e9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" />, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of each. So now, we need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78ed665d4718790e48ff9e7ada4f963dbeb685e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right) + 4\\left(\\frac{y}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"113\" height=\"33\" />. Expanding out the fractions, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b834e2f4283cd094e522a075e53c0e167bc0b66c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right) + 4\\left(\\frac{y}{2}\\right) = 2x + 2y = 2(x + y) = 2(3) = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"383\" height=\"35\" />.\nSo, the area of the square we need is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60a1fea44543488d22920b30432ac9faecadcf11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25- (4+6) = 15\\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"227\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceed as in solution 1 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/166f177e23ef61169a1ed4e1589a8da1eb65a177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 5x + 5 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that the side length of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/2/b62ffb4d959ac3a02739d1b037620dd4fe347270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2+(5-x)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"123\" height=\"35\" /> by the Pythagorean Theorem. Thus, the area of the square is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/219ed858ceeee9961cffb29d8a960ff48a5ef18d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sqrt{x^2+(5-x)^2}\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd07101cf484357063b04a40fad61863fd270664.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= x^2 + x^2 - 10x + 25\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/5351c47c3494a6167c56a7b69ef408a669448473.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (2x^2 - 10x + 10) + 15\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfee2af720d4a20af7d9d8d9ebcd307b0b16e5c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2(x^2 - 5x + 5) + 15\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c7f1b84813de6130c94e71c5aa53c811663c454.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2(0) + 15\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfaff7db0d5104adc924c383e22fb737866e4bb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\boxed{15}\\]\" width=\"48\" height=\"23\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b546baa70412e3982dd1708c27072193bed63f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Fast_with_no_explanations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Fast_with_no_explanations)\">Solution 5 (Fast with no explanations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Fast with no explanations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By inspection, we can see that the area of the largest square would be the area of the middle square formed by the vertices of the shaded squares plus half the combined area of the four smaller rectangles. Our desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3681861a1e2cc08621eb8f1391546edb568467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + \\frac{3\\cdot4}{2} = 15\\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~Irfans123\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rTljQV79PCY\">https://youtu.be/rTljQV79PCY</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/51K3uCzntWs?t=3358\">https://youtu.be/51K3uCzntWs?t=3358</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GrACenkaD8M&amp;t=315s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GrACenkaD8M&amp;t=315s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 8\">2015 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=